# rich-readable

An **instruction**, not a CSS class or a page badge. Write study HTML so it is scan-first: a reader should catch key words and the decision in a few seconds.

Do **not** wrap content in `.rich-readable`. Do **not** use mermaid. Do **not** use ASCII art or `.boxflow`. Use the helpers already in the app.

## Build order

1. **Chips** — `.chips` / `.chip` for the keywords of the page
2. **Tldr** — `.tldr`, one or two sentences, bold the claim
3. **Split prose** — long paragraphs become `.tight` bullets
4. **Highlight** — `<b>`, `<code>`, `<span class="tag">` on terms that must pop
5. **Boxes** — `.scale` > `.pan` for comparisons; `.note` for a trap; `.callout` / `.callout.tradeoff` for a scored line
6. **Diagrams** — inline SVG in `.diagram` + `.diagram-cap`, copied from the **Backpressure** term. Not mermaid. Not ASCII. Not `.boxflow`.
7. **See also** — `<a class="chip" href="#id">` or `#topic/id` / `#qa/id`

## Color roles (existing classes)

- `.go` / SVG `.d-ok` — keep / do this (green `#2e7d32`)
- `.warn` / SVG `.d-accent` — trade-off / signal
- `.trap` / SVG `.d-warn` — don’t (red `#c62828`)

## Diagrams (canonical: term Backpressure)

Every flow, pipeline, fork, or with-vs-without picture is an inline SVG:

- Wrap in `<div class="diagram">`. Caption in `<p class="diagram-cap">`.
- `viewBox="0 0 720 …"` so it scales. `role="img"` + `aria-label`.
- Theme with CSS variables: `var(--text)`, `var(--panel-2)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--accent)`, `var(--accent-soft)`.
- Boxes: `<rect rx="7">` + `.d-lbl` / `.d-sub`. Arrows: `<line>` + a **unique** `<marker id="…-ah">` per diagram (IDs must not collide on the page).
- Row label: `.d-step`. Feedback arc: dashed `var(--accent)` + `.d-fb`. Failure note: `.d-bad`.
- Two-row compare (WITH vs WITHOUT) and a top box forking into options are the usual shapes — see Backpressure “Data path” and “Control flow”.

```html
<div class="diagram">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 720 120" role="img" aria-label="producer to bounded queue" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <style>
      .d-lbl{fill:var(--text);font:600 13px -apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif}
      .d-sub{fill:var(--text);opacity:.78;font:11px -apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif}
      .d-box{fill:var(--panel-2);stroke:var(--border);stroke-width:1.5}
      .d-ok{fill:var(--panel-2);stroke:#2e7d32;stroke-width:2}
      .d-warn{fill:var(--panel-2);stroke:#c62828;stroke-width:2}
    </style>
    <defs>
      <marker id="ex-ah" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="var(--text)"/></marker>
    </defs>
    <rect x="24" y="24" width="160" height="44" rx="7" class="d-box"/>
    <text x="104" y="50" text-anchor="middle" class="d-lbl">producer</text>
    <line x1="184" y1="46" x2="238" y2="46" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ex-ah)"/>
    <rect x="240" y="24" width="160" height="44" rx="7" class="d-ok"/>
    <text x="320" y="50" text-anchor="middle" class="d-lbl">bounded Q</text>
  </svg>
</div>
<p class="diagram-cap"><strong>Bound the queue</strong> so fullness becomes a signal.</p>
```

Walls of prose, mermaid, ASCII flowcharts, and `.boxflow` are out of spec.
